cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "tenantbench: a leakage benchmark for tenant validators of language-model-generated SQL"
abstract: >-
  Corpus, row-level-security oracle and harness for testing SQL validators that enforce a
  tenant predicate on statements written by language models. Twelve structural bypass classes
  are templated onto five BIRD development databases with a synthetic four-tenant split; a
  statement leaks when its PostgreSQL result with row-level security differs from its result
  without it. Includes seven validator adapters, a release-history sweep for two open-source
  validators, a language-model arm under prompt injection, and a semantic-layer run test.
